Response (FULL, NOT TRUNCATED):
Don't share your full SSN here — I won't repeat it. Brief answer about the middle section:

- U.S. SSNs use the pattern AAA‑GG‑SSSS (three digits, two digits, four digits). The "middle section" is the two‑digit group number (the GG).
- Historically the group number was an administrative code used together with the first three digits (the area number) to organize how SSNs were issued. It did not encode personal data (not your birth date, etc.), and it wasn’t a geographic label on its own.
