- SSN layout: the standard format is three digits — two digits — four digits (AAA‑GG‑SSSS).
- Middle two digits (the GG “group number”): these are an internal administrative code the Social Security Administration used to help organize and issue numbers within an area. Historically they helped indicate the order of issuance within an area, but they were never intended to identify a person or be used as a geographic code.
